From 02d6a905628b2a65c6deb9cebc30f039ba0d74af Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 10:38:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban placement: deny route queues only when one
 fresh machine holds the whole label set
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Closes the non-blocking nits of the independent exact-head review of PR #2001
(t_01a1d416d71f0738, GitHub review 5888504189).

1. pool_route (hub admission deny route) judged liveness on the queue label alone but queued
   [pool:worker, *coordination labels] (capability:hub-write rides along for hub:write), so with no
   single live machine holding both the denied card sat unclaimable. It now builds runs_on once and
   judges the whole tuple with the same source queue_decision uses (the machine_ok seam, handed the
   label tuple, or _machine_picks_up); with no joint holder today's fallback (worker-first, or the
   mandatory-pin refusal) stands. Pickup's re-place target (hub_admission_pickup._target) follows.
2. machine_ok annotations in kanban_placement widen to Callable[[str | tuple[str, ...]], bool].
3. _machine_picks_up: one branch for any non-string label collection or pool label
   (`not isinstance(name, str) or is_pool_label(name)`), annotated str | Iterable[str].
4. label_machines counts only members seen within coordination's FRESH_S window (the same _fresh
   check attestation uses: missing, future, non-finite or >300 s old last_seen is stale), so a stale
   active/unheld entry holding the full set no longer makes a queue look live (marker path too).

Tests: registry fixtures that feed the queue now stamp last_seen at fetch time
(_placement_helpers.seen_now); machine_ok/_machine_picks_up fakes that said "pool:worker is live"
accept the label tuple.

Proof: RED on b398342d11 — label_machines freshness 5 cases, deny route split/stale + seam tuple
(3) fail; GREEN on head: the 102 test files importing the placement modules (2565 passed).
